From 18c45b361e952c6dbdcfa2b9b7fc2257156ccead Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 18:03:44 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] documents: hold an upload with no content type to the
 allow list

The upload validator skipped the MIME allow list when the declared content
type was empty, so a multipart part or upload session without a
Content-Type stored any file the extension blocklist did not name.

The validator now resolves the media type: the declared type without its
parameters, or the type the file name's extension maps to when none was
declared. A file whose type cannot be determined, or whose type the allow
list does not name, is refused, and the upload, store and session paths
keep the resolved type rather than the raw header.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01L7Gd5v8t2y7WHswGwtgbrn
