+A person reads a document only through `documentports.DocumentReadAccess`
+(`documents/app/documentaccess`): they hold `document:read`, they may read the record the
+document belongs to (`document.OwnerResource`, stored on the row as the generated
+`documents.owner_resource` column), and a file attached to an assistant conversation is read
+only by the conversation's owner. Every documents route that reads one document, its bytes,
+its versions, its extraction or its assistant history, and every one that changes it, checks
+it first; the routes over one record (`/documents/resource/...`, a list or picker filtered to
+a record) check the record; and an unfiltered list or picker filters in SQL to the owners the
+person may read, so its pages and totals stay whole. Mail attachments and invoice
+attachments go through the same check. Documents are never handed out as presigned URLs:
+every object is a sealed blob, so a presigned URL would serve ciphertext, and the content is
+streamed through the API instead.
+
+`documentservice` records every download and view as a non-critical entry with operation
+`read` and `metadata.access` (`download`/`view`) and `metadata.channel`
+(`content`/`preview`/`page_image`). Because it is in the service, invoice share links, the
+driver portal (a policy's document streams through `GET /portal/policies/:id/document/`) and
+attachment reads are covered as well as the documents API.
